{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevWindowSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevWindowSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevRatioExpansion","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_window_sandwich","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_window_sandwich","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevWindowSum.lean#L110-L143","doc":"**The sandwich, as a ratio.**  The window sum is within `e^{±B}` of the\nmodel — the form the Laplace step consumes, since `e^{B} → 1` exactly when the\nexpansion's error does.\n\nNo sign hypothesis on `B`.  A first draft carried `0 ≤ B`, on the reasoning\nthat `e^{B} − 1` had better be nonnegative; it is not needed, because the step\nthe lower half actually rests on is `e^{B} + e^{−B} ≥ 2`, which holds for EVERY\nreal `B`.  (And a negative `B` forces `s` empty, since `h` would bound an\nabsolute value below zero — so both sides are `0` and the statement is true\nthere too.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_of_log_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_sum_kashaevProd_of_log_bound","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevWindowSum.lean#L89-L108","doc":"**The window sum from below**, the mirror. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_le_of_log_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_kashaevProd_le_of_log_bound","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevWindowSum.lean#L67-L87","doc":"**The window sum from above.**  `e^{B}` factors out of every term, so the\nwhole window is `e^{B}` times the model sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_bounds_of_log_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_bounds_of_log_bound","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevWindowSum.lean#L47-L65","doc":"**The exponentiated ratio, both directions.**  `T` is any target and `B`\nany bound on the discrepancy; the conclusion brackets `g_{k'}` between two\nmultiples of `g_k`.\n\nStated with `T` and `B` abstract so that a sharper expansion can be dropped in\nwithout touching this proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_eq_mul_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_eq_mul_exp","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevWindowSum.lean#L36-L45","doc":"`g_{k'} = g_k · e^{log g_{k'} − log g_k}` — the identity the whole file\nrests on, and the only place positivity of both terms is used. ","signatureChunk":0}]}